{"file": "ministry_of_culture__ministry-of-culture-film-department-eti-cohen__manual.md", "url": "manual://ministry-of-culture/film-department/eti-cohen", "source_name": "ministry_of_culture", "status": "ok", "content_hash": "4bb2d5b2ba32ff679e56be6eb20babad", "content_length": 868, "filter_info": {"reason": "manual_canonical_source"}, "truncated": false, "elapsed_sec": 0, "data": {"metadata": {"source_url": "manual://ministry-of-culture/film-department/eti-cohen", "source_name": "ministry_of_culture", "extraction_date": "2026-05-24", "language": "he", "canonical_source": "FIW article Apr 2024 (unverified by independent source); OSINT 2026-05-24"}, "entities": {"people": {"person_001": {"name_he": "עטי כהן", "name_en": "Eti Cohen", "aliases": [], "primary_roles": ["government_official"], "gender": "f", "notes": "Director of Film Department at Israeli Ministry of Culture 1999–2021 (per FIW allegations; not independently confirmed by mainstream source). Oversaw the Film Council. FIW alleges: passed inside Ministry information to Giora Eini (Rabinovich Fund CEO); allegedly had romantic relationship with Eini; allegedly manipulated Film Council meetings to favor Rabinovich and Gesher funds; allegedly omitted her name from council meeting records. Criteria changes in 2014 and 2019 resulted in significant funding increases to Rabinovich (+9%/+29%) and Gesher (+149%/+82%). Source reliability: FIW article only — not corroborated by independent Israeli source as of 2026-05-24.", "sources": ["manual://osint/fiw-articles-2026-05-24"]}}, "organizations": {}, "films": {}, "events": {}}, "roles": [], "relationships": []}}
